(You do not need to do the math. Just state the big-O.)
Unless otherwise stated, recall that \lq\lq runtime" means \lq\lq worst
runtime".
Also, recall that for recursion runtimes:
\begin{enumerate}[nosep]
\item If the recursive runtime has the form
\[
T(n) = T(n/2) + A
\]
where $A$ is a constant, then
\[
T(n) = O(\lg n)
\]
\item And if
\[
T(n) = 2T(n/2) + An + B
\]
where $A,B$ are constants, then
\[
T(n) = O(n \lg n)
\]
\end{enumerate}

